{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"451ae9891f6725f72cbd8f16340ce3314b25a347b5fb167318ee573b46400f37","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP writes adapter / ticket unlinking","key_entities":["src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets","src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py::unlink","src/rebar/_commands/unlink.py","docs/mcp-reference.md","scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py","relation parameter"],"problem_keywords":["mcp","unlink_tickets","relation selector","parameter parity","write surface","fastmcp schema","ticket linking"],"propositions":["MCP unlink_tickets callable signature and FastMCP schema both omit the optional relation parameter supported by the public library and CLI.","When a ticket pair holds multiple relations (e.g. blocks and relates_to) and MCP receives an explicit relation, the pair-scoped fallback incorrectly removes the most-recent edge instead of the specified relation.","The relation parameter must be added to the MCP callable signature, forwarded unchanged to rebar.unlink, and documented to achieve total library/CLI/MCP write-parameter parity.","When relation is omitted, the documented pair-scoped most-recent fallback behavior must be preserved.","The live FastMCP schema must advertise relation as an optional string-or-null type matching the library contract."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787092572290966001,"uuid":"e305aae1-09a6-4cfc-9f0b-bed1493d9a0a"}